Interstellar by Hazel Quantock (TekF)
https://www.shadertoy.com/view/Xdl3D2

The author's notice in the shader reads: "This code is licensed under the CC0
license http://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/"

Where that statement appears: lines 1 to 3 of the shader's own header
("// Interstellar", "// Hazel Quantock", then the sentence above), in
https://raw.githubusercontent.com/y4my4my4m/kde-shader-wallpaper/HEAD/package/contents/ui/Shaders/Interstellar.frag
That copy was used as the source for this port; the Shadertoy page itself could
not be fetched automatically, so the line was not cross-checked there. The
header is the same in the copy as first added to that repository (commit
734aec6a, restored from its older 3.x sources) and in the current one. The
host repository is GPL-3.0 as a whole; this shader carries its own, separate
CC0 notice, and the one edit that repository made to the file (a hash in place
of the noise texture) was not used here: the hash in this port is written anew.

Ported to Metal Shading Language for MacOS Live Wallpaper; see the note at the
top of main.metal. What was changed from the original:

  - mainImage's output parameter is declared the Metal way (thread vec4&).
  - The noise texture on iChannel0 (Shadertoy's 256x256 RGBA noise) is replaced
    by an integer hash that gives one independent random vec4 per grid cell.
    Only its .x was ever used. The unused Rand() function, which read the same
    texture, is left out. No image is shipped with this scene.
  - The animation clock is run at 0.3 of the author's speed (TIME_SCALE), so
    one surge and stall of the fly-through takes about 42 seconds instead of
    12.6 and the fastest streaks do not strobe at a wallpaper's frame rate.
  - The divisor of the ray step is kept off zero, so a pixel exactly at the
    centre of an odd-sized target cannot divide 0 by 0.
  Nothing else: the grid march, its 20 steps, the constants and the colouring
  are the author's.

CC0 1.0 Universal

To the extent possible under law, the author has waived all copyright and
related rights to this work. See
https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/
